# PETSc options for the DIRECTIONAL block Gauss-Seidel PCSHELL preconditioner
# (item 4: exact OpenMP-threaded tridiagonal line solves for the u and v fields).
#
# IMPORTANT run model -- this path does NOT use the MPI linear solver server:
#   * run with a SINGLE MPI rank:   BOUSS_MPI_PROCS = 1   (i.e. mpiexec -n 1)
#   * parallelism is OpenMP over the tridiagonal lines: set OMP_NUM_THREADS
#     to the core count you want (e.g. setenv OMP_NUM_THREADS 6).
# Running with >1 rank here would launch independent duplicate simulations.
#
# point PETSC_OPTIONS at this file:
#   setenv PETSC_OPTIONS '-options_file /path/to/petscOptions_tridiag'

# enable the shell PC (read via PetscOptionsHasName in petsc_driver.f90).
# pc_type is forced to 'shell' in the code, so no -pc_type is needed here.
-use_tridiag_pc

# Krylov solver: GMRES on PETSC_COMM_SELF.  GMRES does the A*x matvec on the
# assembled CRS matrix; the shell PC supplies M^-1 (block Gauss-Seidel with
# exact Thomas line solves).
-ksp_type gmres
-ksp_max_it 200
-ksp_rtol 1.e-9

# print options at end of run:
-options_view

# diagnostics: -log_view crashes at finalize in this build even without the
# server, so leave it OFF.  The code's own end-of-run timing summary
# (Linear solve / Prep-Build / Total, in amr2.f90) gives what we need.
#-log_view
#-ksp_monitor_true_residual
#-options_left
